   "greetings.hello": "Hi! I can help with campus questions: library, deadlines, fees, visas, housing, IT, exams and funding. What do you need?",
   "greetings.bye": "Bye! Come back any time.",
   "gratitude.thanks": "You're welcome.",
   "bot.capabilities": "I'm a small intent-based assistant, not a person and not a large language model. I recognise about a dozen campus topics in English and Persian. When I'm unsure I ask you to choose instead of guessing, and for personal or urgent matters I point you to a human.",
   "library.hours": "Library hours change by term and are extended during exams. The library website lists today's hours and any closures.",
   "admissions.deadline": "Deadlines differ by programme and by funding round. Check the programme's admissions page; funded places often close earlier than the general deadline.",
   "fees.tuition": "Fees depend on the programme and your fee status (home or international). The fees page for your programme lists the amount and the instalment options.",
   "visa.student": "Visa rules are set by the government and change, so I won't guess. The university's international student advice team can check your case; official guidance is on the government visa site.",
   "accommodation.find": "The accommodation office handles university halls and has advice on private renting. Apply early; first-year and international students are often prioritised.",
   "it.wifi": "For Wi-Fi use eduroam with your full university email and password. If your password fails, reset it on the IT self-service page or contact the IT helpdesk.",
   "exams.timetable": "Your personal exam timetable is in the student portal. If you missed an exam or need to change one, contact your school office as soon as possible about special circumstances.",
   "course.registration": "Course selection happens in the student portal during the enrolment window. Your programme handbook lists which courses you can take; your personal tutor can approve changes.",
   "scholarship.funding": "Funding depends on the programme and your fee status. Check the scholarships search and the programme page, and confirm whether a place covers international fees before you apply.",
   "support.wellbeing": "I'm sorry it feels like this. I'm a simple bot and not the right support, but people are: the university wellbeing service offers confidential appointments. If you feel unsafe right now, contact local emergency services.",
   "human.handoff": "The student services desk can help directly; their contact details are on the student support page.",
   "library.location": "The main library's location and the subject libraries are marked on the campus map; search for \"library\" there for directions.",
   "campus.location": "The interactive campus map shows every building and room; your lecture rooms are also listed in your timetable."
  },
